  "title": "Frequency - A Sci-Fi Horror Audio Drama",
  "subtitle": "A sci-fi horror audio drama about radios and neuroscience set in the rural mountains.",
  "description": "After a career-ending scandal, a scientist retreats with her companion AI into the lonely mountains - only to uncover secrets buried in the woods… and perhaps in her own mind. Frequency is an audio horror drama of strange signals, haunted airwaves, and hidden truths. Told through the thoughts of neuroscientist Elise, it follows her struggle to reckon with her past - and the people forever changed by her work. Content Warning: This show contains themes of isolation, paranoia, and horror. Listener discretion advised. If you enjoy The Magnus Archives, Archive 81, or Limetown, and stories that blend psychological dread with technological terror, you’ll want to tune in. But remember- once you start listening, you may not be able to stop.",
